(O/'README.md').write_text('''# Zero-error experimental main-board checkpoint

The approved C27/C31/D5 transaction is integrated atomically on exact r61 with its final 349-pin schematic and project library. Fresh KiCad 10.0.7 refill/DRC has zero errors, zero opens and zero PCB/schematic parity findings. The enabled report retains 54 silk warnings. The separate all-visible PCB report has 11 centering and 5 footprint-type warnings, with no new findings, footprint filters, opens or parity issues. Fresh enabled ERC has zero findings; exposing its four inherited ignored checks produces 13 single-global-label advisories and no errors. No severity settings were weakened.

C27 and added C31 are Samsung CL21A226MAYNNNE, 22 uF, 25 V, C602037 on the exact reviewed minimum-land 0805 footprint. D5 moves only 0.400 mm south. Every original pin/net identity remains; C31 adds two pins, so the fresh map has 349 rather than 347 entries. Exact source-bound WIP BOM/CPL exports use the reviewed main-only part selector and real native position exporter. Their only existing BOM change is C27; only C27 and D5 existing CPL positions change, and C31 is added. These are review outputs, not release CAM.

The complete transaction removes 26 tracks, adds 66 tracks and five explicitly front/back-tented ordinary vias, and relocates six existing vias while retaining their settings. All 26 external ports, all six changed pad entries, every routed via-layer entry and the physical VIN/EN branch cuts pass. All 2,646 unaffected original direct contacts survive. The .500 mm VX feed is preserved with complete via-land coverage; the replacement In1 GND donor is .300 mm, preserving the removed outer donor copper cross-section. No global power-width waiver is used.

Actual refill polygons prove C31, C27, U14, U7 and moved/new GND-via attachments to both main ground planes. All 96 shield-spoke regions survive. Accepted USB copper, all four exact exported taper regions and full-width reference projections remain unchanged. Every original U10/C18/C19 local return path and reference witness survives; the new GND via adds one C18 witness. VIN route projection gaps lie entirely within the explicit transition-via clearance envelopes, with no uncovered mid-corridor area outside them. Finite return topology does not establish return impedance.

Actual exported F/B mask/paste openings change only for the approved C27/C31/D5 footprints. Both new capacitor pad openings are exactly 0.910 by 1.350 mm. All eleven moved/new holes clear every conservative aperture bound by at least 0.130 mm. Sixteen inherited pasted-hole locations, including the U5 thermal-pad process question, remain. The D5 body envelope fits, but its minimum A1 is zero; drill-under-body tenting/seating needs manufacturing qualification.

The C27-to-VIN route improves from 12.271 mm to 9.401 mm, with trace-only nominal resistance falling from 38.04 to 18.52 mOhm. It now uses B/F/B and two through transitions. C31 shares this feed; summed static capacitance is not a claim of high-frequency local decoupling. The C18-to-U10 upstream witness grows from 26.277 mm to 29.803 mm. Exact layer, length, return and resistance tradeoffs are retained in atomic-proposal.json and the independent input-loop review. No additional stability, current, thermal or production qualification is implied.

The main board remains on its original mechanical interface. Corrected mechanical-main and child-board work is separate and must be replayed and validated coherently before fabrication. The canonical reference stays unchanged.

## Diagnostic corrections retained

The historical LDO checker required exact equality of a nearest return-via witness list. It rejected the single additional approved C18 GND-via witness; every original witness was then independently verified unchanged, with a UUID-specific additive allowance. Unset KiCad local mask/paste override getters were distinguished from effective pad openings by the exact Gerber dimensions. Fresh S-expression net export encodes slashes in two inherited unconnected names differently from old XML; only those names are decoded for semantic comparison. A stale recovered design.py export still carried pre-approved C19 metadata; that diagnostic is retained under wip-bom-cpl/rejected-stale-recovery-source, and the accepted source comparison uses exact binding-15 bytes. None of these corrections altered copper or weakened geometric thresholds.
''')
